# AGENTS.local.md — host-specific facts (gitignored)

Copy this file to `AGENTS.local.md` and fill in what applies to **your** machine. An AI agent
working on this repo should, on first run, walk this list with the developer and create the file
(see AGENTS.md §First run). Delete any section that doesn't apply. **Never commit this file** —
`AGENTS.local.md` is gitignored; keep secrets out of it.

## MCP servers available in this environment
<!-- List the MCP servers an agent can use here (playwright is the recommended baseline). -->
- **playwright** (local, browser QA) — recommended harness per AGENTS.md.
- **android-phone** (remote, optional): `http://<PHONE_IP>:8080/mcp` — token at `<TOKEN_PATH>`.

## Device (adb + android-phone MCP — same device, optional)
- `adb devices` shows: `<SERIAL_OR_IP:PORT>` — <device model / Android version>, wifi-adb.
  ⚠ Wifi-adb port drifts across reboots: re-check `adb devices` before device QA.
- Android app under test: `com.yasha.assist` (installed versionName: `<version>`).
  Before assistant-role QA: `adb shell cmd role get-role-holders android.app.role.ASSISTANT`.

## Deployment / URLs
- Stack URL used for QA (desktop and/or phone): `<http(s)://host:port>`
  <!-- Must be reachable from the phone if you do device QA (LAN IP or public dev host). -->
- Lemonade topology (see AGENTS.md §First stack setup):
  - [ ] Bundled (`LEMONADE_BASE_URL=http://lemonade:13305`)
  - [ ] External: `LEMONADE_BASE_URL=<url>` with `lemonade.deploy.replicas: 0` in
        `compose.override.yml`
- Is that Lemonade reachable from the agent/container network? `<yes/no — if no, verify backend
  health through the app (/api/health, /api/lemonade/status, UI badge), never raw curl>`
- `ADMIN_ALLOW_MUTATIONS` in `.env`: `<true/false>` (false = never attempt mutating Lemonade calls)
- Ports in use on this host (avoid conflicts): `<e.g. 80, 443, 3000, 13305>`

### Available users
<!-- Test credentials on the dev instance only. NEVER real passwords or production accounts. -->
- Admin: `<username>` / `<password>`
- Basic: `<username>` / `<password>`
- Test-user naming for scripted QA: prefix `t<phase>_` (AGENTS.md rule 7); DB at `./data/yasha.db`.

## Host notes
- Repo root: `<absolute path>`
- Containers only (docker|podman compose); allowed host tools: git, curl, docker|podman, adb,
  python3 (AGENTS.md rule 2).
- Compose command used here: `docker compose` | `podman compose`
- Anything else agents keep tripping on here: `<free text>`
